  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at the Bowery Ballroom in New York on March 29, 2011, for a show that is the 154th in the archive’s collection for the band [3]. The recommended recording, uploaded by nyctaper, is a matrix mix combining soundboard and audience microphones, capturing 23 songs over 107 minutes [1]. The setlist includes deep cuts like “Home Again Garden Grove” and “Age of Kings,” which are first in the archive, alongside rare tracks such as “Plain” and “Outer Scorpion Squadron” [1][3]. The performance follows a previous archived show at the same venue on March 28, 2011 [3]. One listener, puck2, reviewed this specific recording in 2025, noting that while they could not give everything five stars, they found the banter off-putting and the song choices less than ideal [2]. The recording is rated 3/5 by one listener [1]. A fan art piece for this show is credited to Maryanne Ventrice [4]. The set features a mix of well-known and obscure songs, with “Shower” and “Sinaloan Milk Snake Song” appearing as bustouts after long gaps in the archive [3]. The encore includes “Best Ever Death Metal Band in Denton” and “Palmcorder Yajna” [1].",
